//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="7\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: mem.model.value, abi.native.closure
//! s117 (#136), the same class one constructor over: an s105 closure
//! entry (`main.cls0`) is a `func.addr` referee exactly like a task
//! shim — before s117 the release tier's partitioner saw no edge
//! into it, bin-packed it away from `main`, and the emitter refused
//! `func.addr of @main.cls0 outside this object's subset` while the
//! native tier ran the same program. Probed and pinned by the s117
//! contract: the fix is the summary's `refs=` edge (v3), which
//! covers every `func.addr` construct by construction — spawn was
//! never special-cased. The recursive mills force the multi-cluster
//! partition (see conc/spawn_cluster_split.lu, this file's twin).

